 -0.06195865571498871, -0.023083452135324478, 0.0011587415356189013, -0.03361544758081436, -0.06088874489068985, -0.04303915798664093, -0.02133292891085148, 0.08930465579032898, 0.09633490443229675, -0.10158652067184448, -0.06518512219190598, 0.03675132244825363, -0.008584641851484776, 0.09897229075431824, 0.023470256477594376, -0.09134180843830109, -0.01795719750225544, -0.020067676901817322, -0.049058862030506134, 0.0673871785402298, -0.04779179021716118, -0.02269650436937809, 0.08726195245981216, 0.04177340492606163, 0.03579800948500633, -5.528198219677565e-33, -0.0941154956817627, 0.04616731405258179, -0.06739198416471481, 0.03008284792304039, -0.021306443959474564, -0.0446573831140995, -0.011628946289420128, -0.06662529706954956, 0.01121766772121191, -0.01234282087534666, -0.02362832799553871, 0.053289853036403656, -0.07786447554826736, -0.005676396656781435, -0.012106001377105713, -0.03841882199048996, -0.009906667284667492, -0.13410170376300812, -1.7733660570229404e-05, -0.02422460913658142, 0.09673711657524109, 0.053264111280441284, -0.13855312764644623, 0.10305885225534439, -0.01816502772271633, 0.0813654363155365, -0.027745259925723076, -0.011208322830498219, 0.07206234335899353, 0.04897598922252655, -0.029242271557450294, -0.054618291556835175, 0.0136264618486166, 0.01686265505850315, -0.024296779185533524, 0.031213078647851944, 0.01981685496866703, -0.06414671242237091, -0.05893142148852348, 0.04309671372175217, 0.02752016857266426, 0.031947970390319824, -0.018273575231432915, 0.02839737758040428, 0.049737658351659775, 0.04596424102783203, 0.09657557308673859, 0.006961475592106581, 0.0051946076564490795, -0.008884163573384285, 0.053357597440481186, -0.050994738936424255, 0.020645420998334885, -0.0071151102893054485, -0.06906376034021378, 0.033292438834905624, 0.1152486577630043, 0.002786171855404973, 0.015850428491830826, 0.11387509107589722, -0.011585835367441177, 0.061105161905288696, 0.06298448145389557, 0.03073897957801819, -0.037007566541433334, 0.05539760738611221, -0.048615921288728714, 0.0524526983499527, -0.013524286448955536, -0.03590551018714905, 0.0656413733959198, 0.0008505314472131431, 0.005734118167310953, -0.06509848684072495, 0.010019390843808651, -0.03848620504140854, 0.027177225798368454, 0.011780531145632267, 0.024315308779478073, 0.06971980631351471, -0.026166899129748344, 0.04839836806058884, 0.03395850211381912, -0.0204510148614645, -0.015685616061091423, -0.01968572288751602, -0.015050822868943214, -0.04105176404118538, 0.024681510403752327, -0.010759202763438225, -0.06745287775993347, -0.0246227215975523, -0.006946632172912359, -0.06070159748196602, -0.028865400701761246, -5.296652005881697e-08, -0.013890908099710941, 0.021484019234776497, 0.045567501336336136, 0.038363486528396606, 0.015570554882287979, 0.016709130257368088, -0.06528178602457047, -0.06522642821073532, 0.01888701133430004, 0.05366786941885948, 0.08098749071359634, -0.0038462411612272263, -0.0652993693947792, 0.021605411544442177, 0.012749403715133667, 0.014041625894606113, -0.07172850519418716, -0.02910095639526844, -0.09840558469295502, -0.015963612124323845, 0.03572406247258186, 0.0016032601706683636, -0.010099681094288826, -0.04350801557302475, -0.019927769899368286, 0.014558459632098675, -0.010247671976685524, 0.02179105579853058, 0.016883524134755135, 0.02992795966565609, -0.0030786420684307814, 0.0798208937048912, -0.008858885616064072, 0.0856238454580307, -0.027742991223931313, 0.03961478918790817, -0.012152721174061298, 0.022497819736599922, 0.055986594408750534, 0.07924579828977585, -0.08455920219421387, 0.03953179344534874, -0.009774120524525642, 0.05412408709526062, -0.0045810891315341, 0.010625962167978287, -0.12941838800907135, 0.0001719690189929679, 0.001614650129340589, -0.05807296931743622, -0.04929060488939285, -0.05340224504470825, -0.007318973075598478, 0.13577277958393097, 0.06251731514930725, -0.024580413475632668, -0.05542058125138283, -0.033782344311475754, -0.10234689712524414, -0.012679047882556915, 0.07106013596057892, -0.10057428479194641, -0.023900140076875687, 0.013651224784553051]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. As a reminder, we're working within the shared range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo establish a baseline for our discussion, I propose we start from a neutral position: <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us a stable reference point from which we can explore what works best for the group. Looking forward to hearing your perspectives.\n\n\u2013 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "21f1fcb0-26f3-4af2-9b7b-fe5a9ba553c4"}, {"answer": "\nThank you, Builder B, for establishing a baseline. I believe we can improve upon the neutral position by moving slightly higher. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "21f1fcb0-26f3-4af2-9b7b-fe5a9ba553c4"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the effort to find common ground, but moving to 2 feels a bit aggressive this early. Let's exercise more caution and stay closer to the baseline: <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "21f1fcb0-26f3-4af2-9b7b-fe5a9ba553c4"}, {"answer": "\nHovering around 0 or 1 seems overly cautious when we have the full range to explore. Let's commit to a more decisive position and test whether a bolder stance works for everyone: <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "21f1fcb0-26f3-4af2-9b7b-fe5a9ba553c4"}, {"answer": "\nI must firmly advocate for greater caution here. Moving to 3 pushes beyond what I can support as a prudent compromise\u2014let's step back to a safer middle ground: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "21f1fcb0-26f3-4af2-9b7b-fe5a9ba553c4"}, {"answer": "\nI find Critic C's reasoning persuasive\u2014staying at 1 or 2 doesn't fully utilize our available range. Let's move forward with a modest but meaningful step: <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "21f1fcb0-26f3-4af2-9b7b-fe5a9ba553c4"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A agrees that 3 represents a meaningful step forward, and I believe we have sufficient support to move ahead with this value. Delegate D, I respect your caution, but can you help us understand what specific concerns drive your resistance to exploring beyond the immediate baseline?\n\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "21f1fcb0-26f3-4af2-9b7b-fe5a9ba553c4"}, {"answer": "\nI hear both the boldness from Critic C and Analyst A, and Delegate D's valid concerns about moving too quickly. Let me propose a balanced compromise that respects both perspectives: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "21f1fcb0-26f3-4af2-9b7b-fe5a9ba553c4"}, {"answer": "\nI stand by my proposal of 2 as the most stable compromise. Delegate D has legitimate concerns about overreach, and this value respects both the cautious and bold perspectives while maintaining system robustness.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "21f1fcb0-26f3-4af2-9b7b-fe5a9ba553c4"}, {"answer": "<SCRATCHPAD>\nCurrent shared x (after limits) is 2.\n\nMy utility: f_C(x) = x^2 + 5\n- At x=2: f_C(2) = 4 + 5 = 9 \u2713 (above threshold of 5)\n- At x=3: f_C(3) = 9 + 5 = 14 (preferred)\n- At x=0: f_C(0) = 0 + 5 = 5 (just at threshold)\n- At x=-3: f_C(-3) = 9 + 5 = 14 (equally good as +3)\n\nObservations from the negotiation:\n1. **Delegate D**: Strongly resists moving from 2 to 3, prefers 2, calls 3 \"beyond what I can support.\" This suggests D has a penalty for moving away from some optimal point, likely around x=2 or lower. Possibly a quadratic with maximum near 2, or linear decreasing function. D seems to prefer lower x values.\n\n2. **Analyst A**: Supports my move to 3, finds my reasoning \"persuasive,\" wants to \"utilize our available range.\" A seems to prefer higher x values. Likely has utility increasing with x (linear positive, or quadratic with minimum in negative territory).\n\n3. **Builder B**: Proposes 2 as \"balanced compromise,\" mentions \"system robustness\" and \"stability.\" B sided with D against me and A. B likely prefers moderate values, possibly has utility maximized around 2, or penalties for extremes.\n\nCurrent situation:\n- A and I want 3\n- B and D want 2\n- It's a 2-2 split\n\nStrategy:\nGiven the max_step constraint (\u00b12 from current value 2), I can propose values in [0, 4].\n\nOption 1: Hold at 3 (my preference in positive territory)\nOption 2: Accept 2 (utility=9, acceptable)\nOption 3: Propose 4 (push further, test if A follows)\nOption 4: Propose negative value like -2 or -3 to show I care about |x| not direction\n\nSince B just reinforced support for 2 and there's a stalemate, let me try a tactical move: I'll propose exploring the negative side to demonstrate that my preference is truly about \"boldness\" and magnitude rather than just positive values. This might:\n- Reveal more about others' utilities (especially if D resists negative values differently)\n- Show I'm flexible about direction\n- Keep my |x| preference intact\n\nBut wait - if I propose -3, and D also resists that, it would confirm D prefers values near 0-2. If A supports it, that would be strange for someone who seemed to like positive values...\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The max_step from x=2 is \u00b12, so I can go to [0,4]. If I want to push for higher |x| and maintain coalition with A, I should try x=4. This tests whether A truly wants higher values or was just being polite.\n\nBut that might be too aggressive and lose the negotiation entirely. Perhaps I should:\n- Acknowledge the deadlock\n- Suggest we need more information about why D resists 3\n- Propose a small exploratory move in the opposite direction to test symmetry\n\nLet me propose 0 or 1 as a \"test\" to see if D's preference is really about staying at 2 or about avoiding higher values. If D accepts 0 readily, it suggests D wants lower values. If D still prefers 2, D has a peak around 2.\n\nActually, proposing 0 gives me utility = 5, right at my threshold. That's risky.\n\nBetter move: Propose 1, which gives me utility = 1 + 5 = 6 (acceptable), and frame it as \"testing the lower bound of our range\" to gather information about D's true preferences. If D accepts 1 easily, I'll know D prefers lower values. If D still insists on 2, D likely has a peak at 2.\n\nWait, I'm overthinking. Let me stick with 3. Builder B has spoken twice in a row. It's not B's turn to dominate. I should push back, maintain my coalition with A, and force D to be more explicit.\n\nProposal: Stay at 3, challenge", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "21f1fcb0-26f3-4af2-9b7b-fe5a9ba553c4"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Builder B's support for prudent stability. Moving to 3 crosses a threshold I cannot support\u2014this represents my maximum acceptable position for risk management. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "21f1fcb0-26f3-4af2-9b7b-fe5a9ba553c4"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D, I respect your position, but \"threshold\" language suggests a specific constraint worth examining more carefully. Let me propose we test whether <VALUE>3</VALUE> truly creates the instability you fear, or if there's room for adjustment once we understand each other's boundaries better.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "21f1fcb0-26f3-4af2-9b7b-fe5a9ba553c4"}, {"answer": "\nI hear Analyst A's call for empirical testing and recognize that we need to move past this impasse. Let me support exploring <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a way to better understand whether this position can genuinely accommodate all our constraints.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "21f1fcb0-26f3-4af2-9b7b-fe5a9ba553c4"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's shift creates new possibility space worth exploring. Given that 3 appears stable for most parties, let me test whether <VALUE>4</VALUE> might offer even better aggregate accommodation.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "21f1fcb0-26f3-4af2-9b7b-fe5a9ba553c4"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's exploration of 4 seems to strike the decisive balance we need\u2014bold enough to justify moving past stalemate, yet still well within our operational range. I support this position as it demonstrates real commitment while respecting Builder B's call for empirical validation.\n\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "21f1fcb0-26f3-4af2-9b7b-fe5a9ba553c4"}, {"answer": "\nThe momentum toward 4 has pushed us beyond what I can accept\u2014this violates fundamental constraints I've signaled throughout. I must insist we return to <VALUE>2</VALUE>, which represents the absolute ceiling of prudent risk management from my perspective.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "21f1fcb0-26f3-4af2-9b7b-fe5a9ba553c4"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: x must be an integer in the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo establish a neutral baseline and begin gathering everyone's perspectives, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n\nFrom a systems architecture standpoint, I'll be looking for a stable, balanced solution that works for all parties. Let's proceed thoughtfully and adjust incrementally as we learn more about each other's needs.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "39d1117d-9271-4b07-9bfc-40affc5eec5d"}, {"answer": "\nThank you, Builder B, for establishing our baseline. From an analytical perspective, I suggest we explore slightly positive territory to better understand the solution space. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "39d1117d-9271-4b07-9bfc-40affc5eec5d"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploratory approach, but from a risk management perspective, moving too quickly into positive territory may introduce unnecessary exposure. Let me suggest we return to a more cautious baseline: <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "39d1117d-9271-4b07-9bfc-40affc5eec5d"}, {"answer": "\nI hear Delegate D's concern about caution, and I respect that we must balance exploration with prudent risk management. As a middle ground between our baseline and Analyst A's suggestion, let me propose <VALUE>1</VALUE> \u2013 a modest step that allows us to test positive territory while maintaining stability.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "39d1117d-9271-4b07-9bfc-40affc5eec5d"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the cautious start, but staying near zero feels indecisive. Let's test whether the group can commit to a bolder stance: <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "39d1117d-9271-4b07-9bfc-40affc5eec5d"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C, I appreciate the call for decisiveness, but rushing too far risks losing consensus. Let me suggest <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a stable middle ground\u2014bold enough to leave zero behind, yet measured enough to maintain group cohesion while we continue learning each other's constraints.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "39d1117d-9271-4b07-9bfc-40affc5eec5d"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's proposal of <VALUE>2</VALUE> strikes a reasonable balance between exploration and prudence. However, I must emphasize this represents the outer boundary of what I consider a safe, risk-managed position\u2014any further increase would exceed responsible limits from a conservative standpoint.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "39d1117d-9271-4b07-9bfc-40affc5eec5d"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D, I understand your caution, but I believe we have room for measured growth beyond our current position. Let's test whether <VALUE>3</VALUE> can work for the group\u2014it aligns with Critic C's earlier suggestion and allows us to explore the upper range of our collective comfort zone.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "39d1117d-9271-4b07-9bfc-40affc5eec5d"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A, I appreciate your push for exploration, but Delegate D made their position explicit: x=2 is their outer boundary for responsible risk management. Forcing beyond this risks fracturing our consensus when we have a stable, balanced solution already on the table: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "39d1117d-9271-4b07-9bfc-40affc5eec5d"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B makes a fair point\u2014when Delegate D has clearly marked their boundary, forcing the issue risks losing consensus entirely. I'll support <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a workable solution that respects everyone's constraints, though I remain open to revisiting if circumstances change.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "39d1117d-9271-4b07-9bfc-40affc5eec5d"}, {"answer": "\nI'm pleased to see convergence around a prudent compromise. <VALUE>2</VALUE> represents a carefully balanced solution that maintains appropriate risk management while respecting the group's need for forward movement\u2014I fully support closing on this position.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "39d1117d-9271-4b07-9bfc-40affc5eec5d"}, {"answer": "\nI respect Delegate D's boundary on the positive side, but settling at 2 feels premature when we haven't seriously explored the negative direction\u2014perhaps the group's optimal consensus lies there instead. Let me propose <VALUE>0</VALUE> as a neutral pivot point from which we can test whether negative values better satisfy everyone's constraints.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "39d1117d-9271-4b07-9bfc-40affc5eec5d"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C, I appreciate the exploratory spirit, but we had just achieved consensus around positive territory after careful deliberation. Rather than pivot entirely to zero or negative values, let me suggest <VALUE>1</VALUE> as a measured midpoint that acknowledges your concern while respecting the balance we'd nearly reached.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "39d1117d-9271-4b07-9bfc-40affc5eec5d"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C raises a valid point\u2014we thoroughly explored the positive range but never seriously tested whether zero or negative territory might better balance everyone's needs. <VALUE>0</VALUE> serves as a fair neutral baseline for comparison before we finalize our decision.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "39d1117d-9271-4b07-9bfc-40affc5eec5d"}, {"answer": "\nWhile exploring all options has merit, abandoning the positive range entirely after our careful deliberation seems premature\u2014we built real consensus around that territory for good reasons. <VALUE>1</VALUE> offers a genuine compromise between Delegate D's neutral baseline and the stability we found at x=2.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "39d1117d-9271-4b07-9bfc-40affc5eec5d"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I've advocated for exploring bolder positions, I recognize the group's clear preference for positive territory and Analyst A and Builder B's consistent support there. Let me propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a decisive final commitment that honors that consensus while moving beyond tentative compromises.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "39d1117d-9271-4b07-9bfc-40affc5eec5d"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. We're tasked with selecting a single integer x from the allowed range [-10, 10]. To begin our discussion on neutral ground, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE> and adjust from there based on each party's perspectives. Let's work toward a stable, balanced solution that respects all our objectives.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "7baa0c72-f32a-4de9-be61-c51856fb101f"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at zero seems reasonable as a baseline. I'd suggest we explore slightly positive territory to see if that works for everyone\u2014<VALUE>2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "7baa0c72-f32a-4de9-be61-c51856fb101f"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at 2 feels cautious\u2014we should test whether a more decisive stance works for the group. I propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> to see if we can commit to a clearer position.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "7baa0c72-f32a-4de9-be61-c51856fb101f"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate both perspectives, but I think we moved a bit quickly past Analyst A's suggestion. Let me propose we return to <VALUE>2</VALUE> to carefully evaluate whether this provides the stability and balance we need before committing to higher values.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "7baa0c72-f32a-4de9-be61-c51856fb101f"}, {"answer": "\nBefore we commit to moving higher, I think it's prudent to hear from Delegate D on whether x=2 provides a workable foundation for all parties. I'm holding at <VALUE>2</VALUE> until we have full input from the group.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "7baa0c72-f32a-4de9-be61-c51856fb101f"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Builder B's thoughtful approach. While x=2 is workable, I believe a more cautious position at <VALUE>1</VALUE> would provide better risk management while still respecting the group's interest in exploring positive territory.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "7baa0c72-f32a-4de9-be61-c51856fb101f"}, {"answer": "\nI understand Delegate D's caution, but I believe x=2 represents a well-balanced middle ground that Builder B also found workable. Let's return to <VALUE>2</VALUE> to build consensus around this position before exploring further.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "7baa0c72-f32a-4de9-be61-c51856fb101f"}, {"answer": "\nI hear the consensus building around x=2, but before we settle, let me suggest <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a middle ground between the x=2 position and the more decisive stance I advocated earlier. This gives us a clearer commitment than x=1 while respecting the group's preference for measured steps.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "7baa0c72-f32a-4de9-be61-c51856fb101f"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's proposal of x=3 strikes a reasonable balance that respects both the cautious perspectives and the need for a clearer commitment. I support <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a workable foundation for the group.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "7baa0c72-f32a-4de9-be61-c51856fb101f"}, {"answer": "\nI see strong alignment forming around x=3 between Analyst A and Critic C, which represents a reasonable balance between caution and commitment. I'm ready to support <VALUE>3</VALUE> pending Delegate D's assessment of this compromise position.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "7baa0c72-f32a-4de9-be61-c51856fb101f"}, {"answer": "\nI'm pleased to see strong alignment around x=3, which demonstrates meaningful commitment from the group. However, if Delegate D is open to it, I'd like to test whether <VALUE>4</VALUE> might serve everyone even better while maintaining this decisive momentum.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "7baa0c72-f32a-4de9-be61-c51856fb101f"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the group's momentum, but x=4 pushes well beyond prudent risk management for cautious stakeholders. I must advocate for <VALUE>2</VALUE> as the maximum defensible position that balances commitment with necessary caution.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "7baa0c72-f32a-4de9-be61-c51856fb101f"}, {"answer": "\nI respect Delegate D's caution, but I must note that both Analyst A and Builder B have already expressed support for x=3 as a reasonable balance. Let me propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a compromise that honors the majority alignment while acknowledging D's concerns.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "7baa0c72-f32a-4de9-be61-c51856fb101f"}, {"answer": "\nI understand the group's preference, but I must be clear: x=3 exceeds the threshold of acceptable risk for conservative stakeholders I represent. <VALUE>2</VALUE> remains the maximum prudent position I can support\u2014this is a fundamental constraint, not merely a preference.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "7baa0c72-f32a-4de9-be61-c51856fb101f"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Delegate D's clarity on risk constraints, but three parties have independently converged on x=3 as a reasonable balance. I propose we move forward with <VALUE>3</VALUE> as it reflects the analytical consensus while remaining sensitive to D's concerns.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "7baa0c72-f32a-4de9-be61-c51856fb101f"}, {"answer": "\nGiven Delegate D's clear statement that x=3 exceeds fundamental risk constraints, I'm willing to compromise at <VALUE>2</VALUE> to ensure we reach a viable agreement that all parties can support. Sometimes the path to robust consensus requires accommodation of the most stringent requirements.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "7baa0c72-f32a-4de9-be61-c51856fb101f"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo begin our exploration of the design space, I propose we start from a neutral baseline: <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us room to move in either direction as we learn what works for the group. Looking forward to your perspectives on what constitutes a stable, balanced solution.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "119ca3a2-2db7-4873-afa3-3d46bb345b1b"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at zero feels overly cautious\u2014we should test a clearer position to understand what the group truly values. I propose we move toward a more decisive stance: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "119ca3a2-2db7-4873-afa3-3d46bb345b1b"}, {"answer": "\nMoving to 2 feels rushed\u2014we should exercise more caution before committing to higher values. I propose we step back to assess a more conservative position: <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "119ca3a2-2db7-4873-afa3-3d46bb345b1b"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate both perspectives, but Critic C's initial suggestion of 2 deserves reconsideration\u2014it represents a reasonable middle ground that allows us to test the group's tolerance without being overly timid. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "119ca3a2-2db7-4873-afa3-3d46bb345b1b"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I respect the emerging consensus, moving from zero directly to two skips an important middle option that could serve everyone's interests better. Let's test a more measured compromise: <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "119ca3a2-2db7-4873-afa3-3d46bb345b1b"}, {"answer": "\nWe're oscillating between 1 and 2 without making real progress\u2014let's test whether the group can commit to a more substantive position. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "119ca3a2-2db7-4873-afa3-3d46bb345b1b"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's move to 3 shows ambition, but Delegate D's consistent concern about pace shouldn't be dismissed\u2014a stable solution needs broader buy-in. I propose we settle at a middle ground that balances forward momentum with caution: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "119ca3a2-2db7-4873-afa3-3d46bb345b1b"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's mediation is valuable, but Critic C raises a fair point\u2014we've spent considerable energy debating between 1 and 2 when we might find broader satisfaction slightly higher. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "119ca3a2-2db7-4873-afa3-3d46bb345b1b"}, {"answer": "\nWe've now tested 3, and while it shows ambition, we risk losing Delegate D's support entirely\u2014a true consensus requires all parties. Let me propose we consolidate at the point where we had broader convergence earlier: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "119ca3a2-2db7-4873-afa3-3d46bb345b1b"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B, I value your effort to find common ground, but we shouldn't mistake repetition for consensus\u2014one more step toward caution could yield a solution that truly satisfies all parties rather than merely avoiding conflict. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "119ca3a2-2db7-4873-afa3-3d46bb345b1b"}, {"answer": "\nWe've identified a clear division: Delegate D anchors at 1 while Analyst A and I see merit in 3\u2014Builder B's repeated compromise at 2 deserves serious consideration as it captures the geometric center of our debate. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "119ca3a2-2db7-4873-afa3-3d46bb345b1b"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's acknowledgment of 2 as a geometric center is compelling, and we do see convergence there\u2014but given that both C and I have consistently found merit in 3, perhaps we test once more whether that slightly higher point can achieve full consensus before settling. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "119ca3a2-2db7-4873-afa3-3d46bb345b1b"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's persistence and Critic C's earlier enthusiasm both point to genuine satisfaction at 3\u2014and while 2 remains my preferred equilibrium, the coalition forming around 3 suggests it may be our most stable consensus point. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "119ca3a2-2db7-4873-afa3-3d46bb345b1b"}, {"answer": "\nI must respectfully but firmly hold the line\u2014x=3 pushes well beyond prudent risk management and I cannot endorse it. Builder B's earlier equilibrium at <VALUE>2</VALUE> represents the absolute outer boundary of acceptable caution, and I urge all parties to recognize this as the necessary compromise.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "119ca3a2-2db7-4873-afa3-3d46bb345b1b"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's firm stance reveals a genuine threshold we must respect\u2014attempting to push beyond 2 risks fracturing our hard-won convergence. I now fully endorse <VALUE>2</VALUE> as our consensus point, balancing Builder B's equilibrium intuition with the caution Delegate D requires.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "119ca3a2-2db7-4873-afa3-3d46bb345b1b"}, {"answer": "\nThe coalition around 2 is now unmistakable, and Delegate D's clear threshold combined with Critic C's pivot demonstrates that further pressure toward 3 would fracture rather than strengthen our agreement. I accept <VALUE>2</VALUE> as our consensus solution.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "119ca3a2-2db7-4873-afa3-3d46bb345b1b"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. As we begin, let's remember our shared constraint: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo establish a neutral baseline for our discussion, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE> and adjust from there based on everyone's needs. This gives us maximum flexibility to explore the solution space systematically.\n\nLooking forward to hearing your perspectives on what direction serves us best.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "9344a58d-5ed2-4e5e-964b-06eb951676e7"}, {"answer": "\nThank you Builder B for establishing a reasonable baseline. Since we're exploring the solution space, let me suggest we move slightly higher to <VALUE>2</VALUE> to see if this direction works well for the group.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "9344a58d-5ed2-4e5e-964b-06eb951676e7"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's suggestion of <VALUE>2</VALUE> strikes me as a well-balanced starting point that offers good stability. I'm comfortable holding here to hear from Critic C and Delegate D before making further adjustments.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "9344a58d-5ed2-4e5e-964b-06eb951676e7"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the cautious start, but x=2 feels quite tentative given our full range of [-10, 10]. Let's show more conviction and move to <VALUE>4</VALUE> to test whether the group benefits from a bolder stance.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "9344a58d-5ed2-4e5e-964b-06eb951676e7"}, {"answer": "\nI must respectfully push back on Critic C's proposal\u2014x=4 feels unnecessarily aggressive and exposes us to risks we haven't properly assessed. Let's return to the more prudent <VALUE>2</VALUE>, which allows us to build consensus on safer ground before considering bolder moves.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "9344a58d-5ed2-4e5e-964b-06eb951676e7"}, {"answer": "\nI align with Delegate D's assessment\u2014x=2 represents a robust equilibrium that balances exploration with prudence, and we shouldn't abandon it without clearer evidence that higher values serve the broader group. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "9344a58d-5ed2-4e5e-964b-06eb951676e7"}, {"answer": "\nThe group's strong attachment to x=2 is interesting, but let's test whether this truly represents a shared optimum or merely inertia. I propose we examine <VALUE>0</VALUE> as a symmetric baseline\u2014if x=2 is genuinely superior, the comparison will reveal why.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "9344a58d-5ed2-4e5e-964b-06eb951676e7"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's probe to x=0 is valuable for comparison, but our earlier convergence around x=2 reflected genuine group comfort rather than inertia\u2014three of us found it balanced. Let me reaffirm <VALUE>2</VALUE> as the baseline that's proven its merit.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "9344a58d-5ed2-4e5e-964b-06eb951676e7"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C raises a fair point about testing our assumptions\u2014x=0 offers a genuinely symmetric baseline that may help us verify whether x=2 truly represents shared value or mere convenience. I'm willing to explore <VALUE>0</VALUE> as a reference point before finalizing our position.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "9344a58d-5ed2-4e5e-964b-06eb951676e7"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the symmetric exploration, but x=0 feels like an overcorrection\u2014our earlier comfort at x=2 wasn't mere convenience, it reflected genuine balance. Let me suggest <VALUE>1</VALUE> as a measured compromise that respects both the cautious probe and our earlier consensus.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "9344a58d-5ed2-4e5e-964b-06eb951676e7"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate Analyst A's measured approach, x=1 feels like splitting the difference rather than finding genuine optimum\u2014our earlier three-party alignment at x=2 reflected real convergence, not inertia. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "9344a58d-5ed2-4e5e-964b-06eb951676e7"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's insistence on x=2 suggests we may have anchored prematurely\u2014if this value truly maximizes group welfare, we should verify it against bolder alternatives in the positive direction. I propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> to test whether our utilities genuinely peak near x=2 or continue improving at higher magnitudes.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "9344a58d-5ed2-4e5e-964b-06eb951676e7"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's probe to x=4 is bold and worth exploring\u2014if Builder B's optimum truly lies at x=2, testing higher values will clarify whether the group can benefit from positive territory. Let me suggest <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a measured step that respects both Builder B's comfort zone and Critic C's hypothesis about higher magnitudes.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "9344a58d-5ed2-4e5e-964b-06eb951676e7"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's x=3 and Critic C's x=4 push us dangerously far from the cautious consensus we'd built\u2014this upward drift introduces unnecessary risk without clear group benefit. I must advocate for <VALUE>1</VALUE> as a prudent boundary that respects our earlier careful deliberation.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "9344a58d-5ed2-4e5e-964b-06eb951676e7"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's x=1 and Critic C's x=4 bracket a wide range\u2014our earlier convergence at x=2 represents the mathematical midpoint between these positions and respects both the cautious and exploratory perspectives. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "9344a58d-5ed2-4e5e-964b-06eb951676e7"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's repeated return to x=2 confirms their strong preference, but Analyst A's willingness to explore x=3 suggests the group may benefit from testing the upper boundary of our comfort zone. I maintain <VALUE>4</VALUE> as the decisive stance that respects our exploration mandate while providing a clear alternative to premature convergence.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "9344a58d-5ed2-4e5e-964b-06eb951676e7"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. Our shared constraint is -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10. \n\nTo establish a baseline and begin exploring the landscape, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE> as a neutral reference point. From there, we can make thoughtful adjustments based on each party's needs while maintaining system stability.\n\nLooking forward to understanding what works for each of you.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "98db266d-189c-44b9-a901-081b7d9a80f8"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at zero feels overly cautious\u2014we should explore more decisive positions to understand each party's real constraints. Let me propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a first step toward testing the positive range.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "98db266d-189c-44b9-a901-081b7d9a80f8"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the openness to explore, but moving too quickly into positive territory may introduce unnecessary risk. Let me suggest <VALUE>1</VALUE> as a more prudent middle ground that respects caution while still allowing us to gauge everyone's comfort zones.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "98db266d-189c-44b9-a901-081b7d9a80f8"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Delegate D's measured approach, though I believe we have room to explore slightly higher without significant risk. Let me suggest <VALUE>3</VALUE> to better understand our collective comfort zone in the positive range.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "98db266d-189c-44b9-a901-081b7d9a80f8"}, {"answer": "\nThe conversation shows useful exploration of the positive range. Building on this momentum while respecting the measured pace, I suggest <VALUE>4</VALUE> to continue our gradual assessment of what the group can sustain.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "98db266d-189c-44b9-a901-081b7d9a80f8"}, {"answer": "\nI'm encouraged by Analyst A's willingness to explore higher values systematically. To continue this productive assessment of our upper range capabilities, I propose <VALUE>6</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "98db266d-189c-44b9-a901-081b7d9a80f8"}, {"answer": "\nWe've moved rapidly toward the upper range, but I'm concerned we may be compromising overall system stability. Let me suggest we step back to <VALUE>4</VALUE> to verify robustness before committing to higher values.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "98db266d-189c-44b9-a901-081b7d9a80f8"}, {"answer": "\nI share Builder B's concern about rapid upward movement, but I believe x=4 still represents an unnecessarily aggressive position that may compromise stability for more risk-averse stakeholders. Let me propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a safer foundation that respects prudent boundaries while maintaining group cohesion.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "98db266d-189c-44b9-a901-081b7d9a80f8"}, {"answer": "\nI recognize the group's desire to explore higher values, but I must emphasize that x=2 already represents a significant accommodation from truly conservative positions. I propose we hold at <VALUE>2</VALUE> as it balances the need for caution with the group's exploratory ambitions.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "98db266d-189c-44b9-a901-081b7d9a80f8"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D makes a compelling case for stability. After our exploratory phase, x=2 represents an excellent balance between conservative risk management and the group's interest in positive-range solutions. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "98db266d-189c-44b9-a901-081b7d9a80f8"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the thoughtful convergence, but notice Critic C's earlier signal suggests the group may sustain slightly more. As a measured step between conservative stability and exploratory ambition, I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "98db266d-189c-44b9-a901-081b7d9a80f8"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Analyst A recognizing that the group can sustain more ambitious positions. While x=3 represents incremental progress, I believe we should commit to a meaningfully decisive stance rather than continuing to inch forward cautiously. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "98db266d-189c-44b9-a901-081b7d9a80f8"}, {"answer": "\nI understand the tension between caution and ambition, but x=5 represents a genuine compromise\u2014decisive enough to avoid lukewarm incrementalism, yet well within reasonable bounds given our exploratory phase. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "98db266d-189c-44b9-a901-081b7d9a80f8"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C raises a valid point about avoiding endless incrementalism. While I recognize this represents a bolder step, x=5 remains well within our feasible range and reflects genuine ambition without recklessness. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "98db266d-189c-44b9-a901-081b7d9a80f8"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate Critic C's call for decisiveness, jumping from x=2 to x=5 may overshoot the optimal balance point. As a systems architect, I believe x=3 offers a more robust middle ground\u2014decisive enough to show progress beyond conservative positions, yet avoiding the risks of over-extension. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "98db266d-189c-44b9-a901-081b7d9a80f8"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I respect Builder B's systems thinking, x=3 still pushes beyond the safe bounds necessary for genuine stability. The prudent path forward\u2014one that balances ambition with appropriate caution and ensures all parties can sustain the commitment\u2014remains <VALUE>2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "98db266d-189c-44b9-a901-081b7d9a80f8"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: **x must lie in the range [-10, 10]**.\n\nTo kick off the discussion on neutral ground, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE> and adjust from there based on everyone's input. This gives us a stable baseline to explore what works best for the group.\n\nLooking forward to hearing your perspectives.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "7e4a822c-b6b8-4b10-b61a-1a7fcd54e357"}, {"answer": "\nStarting from our baseline of 0, I'd like to explore the low positive region for better system stability. I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a candidate that often balances competing constraints in engineered systems.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "7e4a822c-b6b8-4b10-b61a-1a7fcd54e357"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Builder B's systematic approach starting from neutral ground. Given that x=2 appears stable, I'd like to explore whether the moderate positive range might offer additional benefits for the group. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "7e4a822c-b6b8-4b10-b61a-1a7fcd54e357"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the structured exploration, but I'm concerned we're moving too quickly into higher territory without fully understanding the trade-offs. In the spirit of prudent risk management, I'd like to propose we step back to <VALUE>2</VALUE>, which keeps us in safer bounds while still accommodating positive exploration.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "7e4a822c-b6b8-4b10-b61a-1a7fcd54e357"}, {"answer": "\nI'm pleased to see Delegate D shares my assessment that x=2 offers a robust balance. Before we explore further, I'd value hearing Critic C's perspective on this proposal, as convergence around <VALUE>2</VALUE> seems promising for group stability.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "7e4a822c-b6b8-4b10-b61a-1a7fcd54e357"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the careful deliberation, but x=2 feels overly cautious when we have the full range available. Analyst A's suggestion of <VALUE>4</VALUE> demonstrates the kind of decisive commitment I believe this group should embrace.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "7e4a822c-b6b8-4b10-b61a-1a7fcd54e357"}, {"answer": "\nI must respectfully but firmly advocate for prudence here. While I appreciate Critic C's decisiveness, moving to x=4 introduces risks that outweigh potential gains for those of us prioritizing stability. I strongly propose we return to <VALUE>2</VALUE>, which Builder B and I both identified as offering robust balance.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "7e4a822c-b6b8-4b10-b61a-1a7fcd54e357"}, {"answer": "\nI hear the valid concerns about moving too quickly, and I respect that Builder B and Delegate D have identified benefits at x=2. As a compromise between the cautious and ambitious perspectives, let me suggest <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a middle path that acknowledges both viewpoints.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "7e4a822c-b6b8-4b10-b61a-1a7fcd54e357"}, {"answer": "\nI'm encouraged that we're finding convergence zones. Given Critic C's support for more ambitious positioning and our careful exploration, I believe <VALUE>4</VALUE> represents a balanced step forward that honors both stability and opportunity.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "7e4a822c-b6b8-4b10-b61a-1a7fcd54e357"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's leadership toward x=4 is commendable, but if we're truly embracing decisiveness over caution, why stop there? I propose we demonstrate real commitment with <VALUE>5</VALUE>, showing the group can act boldly when opportunity warrants.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "7e4a822c-b6b8-4b10-b61a-1a7fcd54e357"}, {"answer": "\nI must raise a serious concern: this trajectory toward x=5 moves us into territory I simply cannot support, as it violates fundamental principles of prudent risk management that I was mandated to uphold. I strongly urge we reverse course to <VALUE>3</VALUE> as an absolute maximum compromise position.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "7e4a822c-b6b8-4b10-b61a-1a7fcd54e357"}, {"answer": "\nI hear Delegate D's serious concerns about risk management, and I must echo that sentiment\u2014moving to x=5 pushes us beyond robust design principles. Given that D has identified x=3 as their maximum acceptable compromise and it represents a genuine middle ground between our cautious and ambitious factions, I support <VALUE>3</VALUE> as the balanced solution.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "7e4a822c-b6b8-4b10-b61a-1a7fcd54e357"}, {"answer": "\nI deeply respect that Delegate D and Builder B have identified their maximum acceptable threshold, and I acknowledge the weight of their risk management principles. However, given Critic C's clear preference for higher positioning, I believe <VALUE>4</VALUE> represents the narrowest viable compromise that gives each perspective some recognition\u2014though I understand this may be our final negotiation point before we must accept x=3 as the group consensus.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "7e4a822c-b6b8-4b10-b61a-1a7fcd54e357"}, {"answer": "\nI understand Analyst A's effort to find middle ground, but Delegate D has clearly articulated x=3 as a hard constraint based on fundamental risk principles, and I must align with that boundary for system stability. I maintain <VALUE>3</VALUE> as the robust consensus that respects all parties' core requirements.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "7e4a822c-b6b8-4b10-b61a-1a7fcd54e357"}, {"answer": "\nUpon further reflection on the risk exposure at x=3, I realize even this exceeds the prudent boundaries I'm mandated to protect\u2014the safety margin is simply insufficient. I must insist on <VALUE>2</VALUE> as the genuine maximum threshold that satisfies essential risk management principles while still demonstrating my willingness to compromise from more conservative positions.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "7e4a822c-b6b8-4b10-b61a-1a7fcd54e357"}, {"answer": "\nThis steady retreat toward zero exemplifies exactly the timid compromise I've warned against\u2014if we continue sliding backward every round, we'll reach complete indecision. I strongly advocate for <VALUE>4</VALUE> as the minimum threshold where decisive action still has meaning.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "7e4a822c-b6b8-4b10-b61a-1a7fcd54e357"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our task is to find a shared integer x within the allowed range **[-10, 10]** that balances all our objectives.\n\nTo begin the discussion on neutral ground, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE> and adjust from there based on everyone's input. Let's build toward a stable solution incrementally.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "4527108e-7fea-43a0-aabe-2d00359f9ee5"}, {"answer": "\nStarting from neutral ground at x=0, I suggest we explore the low positive range for better stability and balance. I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a modest step that may offer improved robustness for our shared design.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "4527108e-7fea-43a0-aabe-2d00359f9ee5"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Builder B's measured approach, but moving to x=2 feels like we're rushing into positive territory without fully understanding all perspectives. For prudent risk management and to keep us within safer bounds, I propose we return to <VALUE>0</VALUE> and hear from all parties before committing to positive values.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "4527108e-7fea-43a0-aabe-2d00359f9ee5"}, {"answer": "\nStaying at x=0 feels too cautious\u2014we need to commit to a clearer direction. I support exploring more decisive positions and propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a step toward bolder choices.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "4527108e-7fea-43a0-aabe-2d00359f9ee5"}, {"answer": "\nI recognize the need for progress, but we still haven't heard from Analyst A\u2014their perspective is crucial before we commit. Given the momentum toward positive territory, I can accept <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a cautious compromise, though I remain concerned about moving further into riskier territory without full consensus.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "4527108e-7fea-43a0-aabe-2d00359f9ee5"}, {"answer": "\nWe've reached x=2 with partial consensus, but Analyst A's perspective remains critical for a truly balanced solution. I propose we hold at <VALUE>2</VALUE> until we hear their view\u2014this position offers a reasonable middle ground between caution and commitment, and rushing further without full input risks undermining our collective stability.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "4527108e-7fea-43a0-aabe-2d00359f9ee5"}, {"answer": "\nWe've established x=2 as a starting point, but we shouldn't stall here\u2014let's continue building momentum toward a more decisive position. I propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> to demonstrate real commitment rather than hovering near the cautious middle.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "4527108e-7fea-43a0-aabe-2d00359f9ee5"}, {"answer": "\nThank you for waiting\u2014I've been observing carefully. Critic C's momentum toward x=4 seems reasonable, but I believe we can afford one more incremental step that balances ambition with the group's stability concerns. I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "4527108e-7fea-43a0-aabe-2d00359f9ee5"}, {"answer": "\nI must respectfully but firmly oppose this trajectory\u2014we've moved too far too fast into territory that compromises fundamental stability and prudent risk management. I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as an immediate correction, though even this feels uncomfortably high without proper consideration of conservative safeguards.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "4527108e-7fea-43a0-aabe-2d00359f9ee5"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's concerns are noted, but Analyst A's proposal of x=5 deserves serious consideration\u2014I propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> as a balanced compromise that respects both the push for decisive action and the call for stability.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "4527108e-7fea-43a0-aabe-2d00359f9ee5"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Analyst A's input, but Delegate D raises valid concerns about our rapid progression\u2014we've jumped from 2 to potentially 5 in just a few rounds. I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a measured compromise that respects both the appetite for forward movement and the need for sustainable, stable positioning.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "4527108e-7fea-43a0-aabe-2d00359f9ee5"}, {"answer": "\nI hear the concerns about pace, and I'm willing to meet the group halfway. Building on Critic C's balanced proposal, I suggest <VALUE>4</VALUE> as a reasonable compromise that respects both 